#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/resume-suspend-troubleshooting.rst:143
#: 17f4ce173d7e4f0ea141a6cf5958fa1e
msgid "Power consumption increases on suspend/resume"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/resume-suspend-troubleshooting.rst:146
#: 2563d0197c11416492cffdd0eb3e0fe3
msgid ""
"This problem is related to the software method used to disable sibling "
"threads and how it interacts with suspend/resume. To solve the problem, "
"disable hyper-threading in the BIOS. This `external guide <https://www.pcmag."
"com/news/how-to-disable-hyperthreading>`__ explains how to disable hyper-"
"threading. Since Qubes does disable hyperthreading by default (by not using "
"secondary threads), you won’t pay any performance cost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/resume-suspend-troubleshooting.rst:149
#: 963ae67a82444f2ab0bb144708ae9b74
msgid "Attached devices in Windows HVM stop working on suspend/resume"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/resume-suspend-troubleshooting.rst:152
#: 6cf671fafd874a26baecfa37439f286c
msgid ""
"After the whole system gets suspended into S3 sleep and subsequently "
"resumed, some attached devices may stop working. To make the devices work, "
"they should be restarted within the VM. This can be achieved under a Windows "
"HVM by opening the Device Manager, selecting the actual device (such as a "
"USB controller), ‘Disabling’ the device, and then ‘Enabling’ the device "
"again. This is illustrated on the screenshot below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/resume-suspend-troubleshooting.rst:154
#: a8f725cc0211423798fe2f901c46c090
msgid "r2b1-win7-usb-disable.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/resume-suspend-troubleshooting.rst:160
#: 5eeb74262fa34906aeb4b1bae57ece52
msgid "Suspend turns off the screen and gets stuck"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/resume-suspend-troubleshooting.rst:163
#: 70e6db4c8c59423d9d36f4b6b38f59d5
msgid ""
"On some devices suspend-to-RAM does not work and a hard power-off is needed "
"to recover, because the system does not go into deep sleep. To get suspend "
"to work, you need to add ``mem_sleep_default=deep`` kernel option. Add it to "
"the ``GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX`` setting in ``/etc/default/grub``, update the grub "
"config, and reboot."
msgstr ""
